A required field that is not a bool, named bare as a when. A bare reference
is a presence test for an optional field and a value for a required bool;
anything else is not a condition.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	name: string
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	name:  string
	count: int
}

ForwardLens: (prev): {
	self: {
		count: 0
	}
	lacunas: {
		count: [{
			type:    Placeholder
			message: "0 is a placeholder"
			when:    prev.name
		}]
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	name:  string
	count: int
}
-- out/error --
error[E0422]: prev.name is string, not a condition
  --> history/1.0.thema:14:13
   |
14 |             when:    prev.name
   |                      ^^^^
   |
   = help: compare prev.name to a value, or name an optional field bare to test whether it is present
